// Raspberry Pico + the non-striped SRAM bank windows (0x2100_0000-0x2103_FFFF)
// that the banked linker script (BLD-002) places everything into. The stock
// platform only maps the striped window at 0x2000_0000.
//
// Modeled as real MappedMemory (not an alias): SRAM3 hosts SRAM-executed
// code (BLD-001) and Renode CPUs execute from mapped memory only. Firmware
// and bootrom never address the same bytes through both windows, so the
// missing stripe-interleave coherence is irrelevant functionally.

using "../external/renode-rp2040/boards/raspberry_pico.repl"

sram_banked: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x21000000
    size: 0x40000
